# AUTHORS
#
# Everyone who has contributed to this tree, in the order they first did, one
# `Proper Name <address>` per line.
#
# This file is a **record and a courtesy**.  It exists so a reader can see who
# built the tree, and so a contributor is named for their work.  It carries no
# legal weight: `NOTICE` states the copyright holder and the licence, and the
# licence of a contribution is the one its commit was made under.  A name here
# is not a copyright claim and grants nothing.
#
# It is also **not** responsibility.  Who reviews which part of the tree now is
# `MAINTAINERS`, and the two answer different questions: a contributor who has
# moved on stays here, and a maintainer who takes over a subsystem is an entry
# there.
#
# A name is added in the commit that first carries it.  When a person has
# committed under more than one address — an address that changed, a work one
# beside a personal one — the canonical form is `.mailmap`'s, which is the file
# `git shortlog`, `git log` and `git blame` actually read.  This list stays the
# record; that file is what makes the record agree with the history.

Raiden Lumine <2557597107@qq.com>
